# Phase 1 — rating storage + write path (ACT)

## Context

- Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md`, requirements 1–4 and their acceptance criteria.
- `src/store.js` (41 lines) — the in-memory store. `messages` is the existing pattern for a
  per-ticket side-table (`Map<ticketId, ...>`); ratings follow the same shape.
- `src/portal.js` (31 lines) — `reply` (lines 21–28) is the closest existing analogue: it
  calls `getMyTicket` for the existence/org check, then branches on `t.status`. `rateTicket`
  follows the same shape but does not reopen the ticket.
- `src/tickets.js:42` — `reopenTicket` already guards `notifyAgent` behind
  `if (t.assignee_id && ...)`, i.e. this codebase already treats "no agent assigned" as
  "skip the notify", not an error. `rateTicket`'s low-score notify reuses that guard.
- `src/notify.js` — `notifyAgent(store, agentId, event)` throws if `agentId` is falsy, and
  `queue` is a **module-level singleton**, not per-store. Every test that checks notifications
  must call `drain()` first, or an earlier test's queued email leaks in. The existing tests in
  `test/tickets.test.js` already do this (e.g. line 26); the new ones below follow suit.

## Requirements covered

1 (rate a resolved ticket 1–5), 2 (one rating per ticket), 3 (own-org only), 4 (notify on 1–2).

## Files

- Modify `src/store.js` — add a `ratings` Map and three methods.
- Modify `src/portal.js` — add `rateTicket`.
- Modify `test/tickets.test.js` — seven new test cases, appended at the end.

