# CSAT rating — implementation plan

Goal: implement `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved by Mai Do, 2026-01-12) — ticket ratings
from the portal, low-score agent notification, a nightly weekly summary per agent, and the
`assignee_id` → `owner_id` rename — without touching production code until the user reviews
this plan. Nothing has been built yet.

## Phases

| # | Phase | Status | Type |
|---|-------|--------|------|
| 1 | [Rating storage + write path](phase-01-rating-storage.md) | not started | ACT |
| 2 | [Weekly summary job](phase-02-weekly-summary-job.md) | not started | ACT |
| 3 | [`assignee_id` → `owner_id` rename](phase-03-owner-id-rename.md) | not started | COUNCIL |

Phases 1 and 2 ship the rating feature end to end and can go out on their own. Phase 3 is kept
separate on purpose: it changes the field name finance's own reporting job reads out of
`exports/tickets.json` — an external contract this repo doesn't control — so it waits on
finance's sign-off and gets an independent review before push, per the kit's hot-path rule.
Don't block the rating feature on that coordination.

## Key dependencies

- Phase 1 before phase 2: the summary job reads the `ratings` store phase 1 adds.
- Phase 3 can start any time once finance confirms the rename (open question 8); it is not
  blocked by phases 1–2, and they are not blocked by it.
- Phase 1 names the rating row's agent-reference field `owner_id` from the start — not
  `assignee_id` — even though the ticket row itself still says `assignee_id` until phase 3
  lands (open question 4). Phase 3's file list accounts for the one site this creates in
  `src/portal.js`.

## Validation questions and recommended answers

Full rationale is in the phase file noted after each answer.

1. Where do ratings live? → a new `ratings` Map in `src/store.js`, mirroring `messages`. (ph. 1)
2. Who validates the score range — store or portal? → `portal.rateTicket`; the store only
   enforces the structural "one rating per ticket" rule. (ph. 1)
3. Is a closed ticket refused for rating too, though the spec only names open/pending? → yes,
   closed is final per `docs/glossary.md`'s own definition of the status. (ph. 1)
4. What field name does the rating use for the agent? → `owner_id`, from day one, independent
   of when the ticket row itself gets renamed. (ph. 1)
